 # Changelog
 
+## 0.6.1 (unreleased)
+
+Additive release: no existing item changed, so 0.6.0 callers compile and behave unchanged. Written, unverified: not compiled or run.
+
+- **Resident index follows writes (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#418).** `ResidentIndex::new(dimension)`, `upsert(key, vector)` (quantises and inserts or replaces in key order), `remove(key)`, `contains(key)`, `keys()` and `memory_bytes()`. A resident index can now be kept current from the app's own writes instead of re-reading the whole table; `VectorStore::resident_index` stays the bulk load. Quantisation is one shared helper, so an index built row by row equals one built in a single pass.
+- **Filtered nearest (#418).** `ResidentIndex::nearest_where(query, limit, keep)` scores only the rows whose key `keep` accepts (an account, a folder), so `limit` counts accepted rows. `nearest` is `nearest_where` with every key accepted.
+- **ANN / sqlite-vec vec0 (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#496): not added.** The ruling on #496 makes the resident int8 index the single owner and requires MailRight to measure it at 160k rows before any sqlite-vec `vec0` backend is considered; `vec0` would also add a native SQLite extension. Nothing is changed for it here.
+- Already in 0.6.0, no change: `bundle_files` (#565), `installed_model_dir` (#582), `reciprocal_rank_fusion` and `RRF_K` (#496). `rightkit-search` 0.4.1 also carries a pure rank-fusion module (with weights) for callers that fuse BM25 with these results.
+
 ## 0.6.0 (2026-10-17)
 
 - **Resident int8 vector index.** New `ResidentIndex` (`src/resident.rs`) and `VectorStore::resident_index(model_id)`: one read of a model's vectors into memory, each row quantised to `i8` with one `f32` scale (`absmax / 127`). `ResidentIndex::nearest(query, limit)` scores by cosine on the dequantised rows and orders ties by key, like `VectorStore::nearest`, without a SQLite scan per query. It is a snapshot: later writes are not seen. Written, unverified: not compiled or run.
