 # Changelog
 
+## 0.4.1 (unreleased)
+
+Additive release: every item below is new; no existing item changed, so 0.4.0 callers compile and behave unchanged. Nothing here was compiled or run locally; CI is the compiler.
+
+- **BM25 ranking (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#418).** New `bm25` module: `tokenize(text)` (folded runs of alphanumerics), `Bm25Params { k1, b }` (defaults 1.2 and 0.75; `Bm25Params::new` sanitises), and `Bm25Index<K>` (`insert`, `insert_tokens`, `remove`, `contains`, `len`, `score`, `search(query, limit)`), an in-memory Okapi BM25 ranker for result sets that are not in an FTS5 table. Ties order by key.
+- **FTS5 index management and ranking (#418, feature `sqlite`, on by default).** New `fts5` module: `Fts5Table` defines an FTS5 table in three layouts (own content, `external_content(table, rowid_column)` projection of a source table, `contentless`) with `tokenizer`, `prefixes` and `contentless_delete`; `create_sql`, `trigger_sql` (the three insert/update/delete triggers of a projection), `ensure`, `exists`, `drop_table`, `rebuild`, `optimize`, `integrity_check`, `index_row`, `remove_row`, `bm25_expr(weights)`, `ranked_sql(weights)` and `search(conn, match_expr, weights, limit)` returning `Fts5Hit { rowid, score }` (higher is better, the negation of SQLite's `bm25()`). Names are checked as plain identifiers and the tokenizer spec is restricted, so no caller string reaches SQL; the `MATCH` expression and row values are bound parameters. `Fts5Error` is `#[non_exhaustive]`. Pair with `Query::fts()` to get the `MATCH` expression.
+- **`html_to_text(html)` (#418, folded in from #495).** Strips tags; skips `script`, `style`, `head`, `template` and comments; turns block elements and `<br>` into line breaks; decodes common named and all numeric character references; collapses whitespace. Total: malformed markup never fails.
+- **Rank fusion (#496).** New `fusion` module: `reciprocal_rank_fusion(&[&[K]], k)`, `weighted_reciprocal_rank_fusion(rankings, weights, k)` and `RRF_K` (60), pure and std-only, for merging a lexical ranking (BM25, FTS5) with a semantic one. `rightkit-embed` 0.6.0 already carries an equivalent unweighted function; the search crate is the owner the #496 ruling names, and the embed copy stays so no dependent changes.
+- **Workspace regex content search (#580, opt-in feature `workspace-grep`, adds `regex` and `sha2`).** New `grep` module: `grep_page(root, files, &GrepRequest, &CancelToken) -> GrepPage` runs one page of a line-regex search in three modes (`Content` with context lines, `FilesWithMatches`, `Count`) under a `GrepBudget` (results, bytes per file and per page, files, deadline), ends with a `GrepStatus` (`Complete`, `Truncated`, `Cancelled`, `Deadline`) and a `GrepCursor` that resumes at the exact line. The cursor is bound to the root and the search (pattern, case, mode, context, glob) by SHA-256 and a mismatch is `GrepError::CursorMismatch`; text form via `encode` / `decode`. Optional `*`, `**`, `?` glob filter. Paths are validated (no absolute, no `..`), symbolic links, binary (NUL in the first 8 KiB), oversize and unreadable files are skipped and counted. **The file list is the caller's:** the `.gitignore`-aware walk is the separate owner of Orthic-Labs/rightkit#417 and is not implemented here.
+- **Already shipped in 0.4.0, no change here:** keyset paging with a lookup-resolved tiebreak, a range bound and a CTE-embedded `LIMIT` (#598: `Keyset::range_bound`, `Keyset::cursor_expr`, `Compiled::page_clauses`), and parent-row (thread) scope bindings (#166, #172: `ChildScope`, `Binding::SqlMulti`, `Binding::SqlByShape`).
+- **Tests:** unit tests in each new module (`bm25`, `fts5` over in-memory SQLite, `html`, `fusion`, `grep` over temp directories).
+
 ## 0.4.0 (2026-10-17)
 
 - **Keyset paging (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#598):** `Keyset::range_bound()` (opt-in, no public field added) adds a redundant bound on the first sort column when a cursor is given (`<=` for `desc`, `>=` for `asc`), so an index on that column can seek to the page. It selects no row the cursor predicate would not; without a cursor nothing is added.
